# AI Rules for Game Stats Tracker (Cursor & Coding Assistants)

## Tech Stack
- Flutter 3.x / Dart 3.x (Null-Safety)
- flutter_riverpod 2.x (State management)
- isar 3.1.0+1 (Fast local embedded NoSQL database)
- Material 3 Design System

## Architecture & State Management
- Use `ConsumerWidget` or `ConsumerStatefulWidget` for UI components.
- Do NOT call `DatabaseService` methods inside `build()` directly without Riverpod.
- Always access mutations via `ref.read(databaseProvider)` and observe streams via `ref.watch(matchRecordsProvider)`.
- Explicitly type all dialogs/routes: `showModalBottomSheet<void>(...)`, `MaterialPageRoute<void>(...)`.

## UI & Styling Guidelines
- **Round Avatars**: All avatars and game thumbnails must be circular (`CircleAvatar` + `ClipOval(child: Image.file(...))`).
- **No Hero Animations**: Do not wrap thumbnails in `Hero` widgets.
- **Image Performance**: Always set `cacheWidth: 100-200` and `gaplessPlayback: true` on `Image.file(...)`.
- **Material 3 Tokens**:
  - Never use `.withOpacity()`; always use `.withValues(alpha: 0.x)`.
  - Use `theme.colorScheme.surfaceContainerHighest` and `theme.colorScheme.surface`.

## Isar Code Generation
- When modifying models in `lib/data/models/`:
  Run: `flutter pub run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs`

## Quality Checks
- Before finishing any task, run `flutter analyze` and `flutter test` to ensure 0 errors.
